-- title:
--   Deligne–Serre realisation inside the q-new trace kernel
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number and $q$ a prime, and let $A$ be an Atkin–Lehner datum for $(M,q)$, that is, a natural number $R$ together with a factorisation $M = qR$ and integers $a,b$ with $qa - Rb = 1$. Write $\mathbb{T} =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 {ℓ | ℓ ∣ M}`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) for the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(M))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid M$ (the excluded set $\{\ell \mid \ell \mid M\}$ removes all $U$-generators, so this is the anemic algebra). Let $\mathfrak{p} \subseteq \mathbb{T}$ be a prime ideal with the property that every $T \in \mathbb{T}$ annihilating the intersection of the kernel of the trace map [`CuspForm.traceLin A hq`](def/CuspForm_LevelLoweringTrace.html#L18) ($f \mapsto f + U_q(f \mid W)$, a cusp form of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(R)$) with the kernel of that trace composed after the Atkin–Lehner operator [`CuspForm.atkinLehnerLin A 2`](def/CuspForm_AtkinLehnerOperator.html#L41) ($f \mapsto f \mid_2 W$) lies in $\mathfrak{p}$. Then there exist $f \in S_2(\Gamma_0(M))$ which is a normalised eigenform in the sense of `IsNormalizedEigenform` (first $q$-expansion coefficient $1$, multiplicativity of coefficients at coprime indices, and the weight-$2$ prime-power recursions $a_{p^{r+2}} = a_p a_{p^{r+1}} - p\,a_{p^r}$ for $p \nmid M$ and $a_{p^{r+2}} = a_p a_{p^{r+1}}$ for $p \mid M$), and a ring homomorphism $\chi$ from $\mathbb{T}$ to the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}$ in $\mathbb{C}$, such that $\chi(T_\ell) = a_\ell(f)$ for every prime $\ell \nmid M$, $\ker \chi \subseteq \mathfrak{p}$, and $a_q(f)^2 = 1$.
--
--   This is the Deligne–Serre lifting lemma applied to the anemic Hecke algebra acting on the $q$-new subspace cut out as the intersection of the two trace kernels: a prime of $\mathbb{T}$ supporting that subspace is realised by an integral normalised eigenform of level $M$ whose eigencharacter is contained in the given prime, the conclusion $a_q(f)^2 = 1$ recording $q$-newness. It supplies the witness extraction step used by [`LevelRaising.exists_isNormalizedEigenform_isNewAt_congr_of_qNewSupport_comap`](thm.html#LevelRaising.exists_isNormalizedEigenform_isNewAt_congr_of_qNewSupport_comap).
